---
---
<section id="how-it-works" class="border-b border-rule px-6 py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Sharing model</h2>
    <p class="mb-10 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-mid">
      Every board has a slug and an edit token. The token lives in the URL fragment — browsers never send fragments to the server, so it stays private until the client deliberately sends it when saving.
    </p>

    <!-- URL anatomy -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <div class="border-b border-rule px-5 py-3">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-subtle">Board URL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="px-5 py-5 overflow-x-auto">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm sm:text-base whitespace-nowrap">
          <span class="text-subtle">https://your-server</span><span class="text-ink font-semibold">/b/kitchen-board</span><span class="text-subtle">#</span><span class="text-pine-600 font-semibold">abcdef123456...</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid border-t border-rule sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="border-b border-rule px-5 py-4 sm:border-b-0 sm:border-r">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-pine-600">with #token → edit</p>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-mid">Anyone with the full URL can change the board. Treat it like a password.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-subtle">without #token → view only</p>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-mid">Anyone can see it. No one can change anything.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        { n: '1', title: 'Create a board',         body: 'Open the directory, keep the suggested slug or pick your own.' },
        { n: '2', title: 'Bookmark the edit URL',  body: 'The returned URL with the #token is your edit link. Save it.' },
        { n: '3', title: 'Share a read-only link', body: 'Same URL, remove everything from # onward. View-only.' },
      ].map((step) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface p-5">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-pine-600">{step.n}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mid">{step.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-subtle">
      Lost the edit token? Recover it from <code class="font-mono text-xs text-ink">data/fridges/&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> — look for <code class="font-mono text-xs text-ink">"editToken"</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
